menu "Tests"

config OPENEMBER_ENABLE_TESTS
    bool "Build and register tests (test/)"
    default n
    help
      When enabled, CMake sets TESTS_ENABLED and builds executables under test/,
      registers them with CTest (ctest / make test).
      Native Linux builds also register process integration tests when their
      service and example targets are enabled. These tests require Python 3.
      Disable for production or embedded images where tests are not needed.

endmenu
